  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Medical and Nutritional Aid to Vulnerable Migrants Crossing the Darien in Panama</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over 458,000 migrants braved crossing the Darien jungle between January and October 2023. By year&apos;s end, Panama is likely to exceed 500,000 entries through the Darien. Darien is one of the world&apos;s most dangerous migration routes where migrants are exposed to natural hazards characterized by the jungle&apos;s tropical wilderness, steep mountains, rivers, and wild animals, as well as criminal groups known for perpetrating violence. 
 
Through this project, IOM aims to provide life-saving humanitarian assistance to migrants who crossed the Darien jungle and are in vulnerable situations through the procurement and distribution of infant formulas (each infant formula package will be distributed with a baby bottle and a water bottle) and non-food items (NFIs), as well as the procurement of medicines that are being donated to health centres managed by the Ministry of Health who will be responsible for distributing these to vulnerable migrants in transit or stranded.</narrative>
  </description>
